  "extraction_notes": [
    "The transfer, output, capacitance, and source-drain diode curves were read directly from the published typical plots.",
    "The published p. 2 table explicitly gives Ciss = 4057 pF, Coss = 603 pF, and Crss = 161 pF, all typical at TJ = 25 degC, VGS = 0 V, VDS = 25 V, f = 1.0 MHz; p. 4 Fig. 5 repeats VGS = 0 V and f = 1 MHz and defines Ciss = Cgs + Cgd with Cds shorted, Crss = Cgd, and Coss = Cds + Cgd. Retain these PDF values: the catalog's 4.057 nF and 603 pF appear to map to Ciss and Coss rather than Coss and Crss, not to a transcription error.",
    "RDS(on) is a maximum of 0.04 ohm at VGS = 10 V and ID = 28 A; no typical tabulated RDS(on) is published.",
    "The datasheet also publishes Qg = 234 nC, Qgs = 38 nC, and Qgd = 110 nC at ID = 28 A, VDS = 160 V, VGS = 10 V; gate charge is not represented by the strict extraction schema.",
    "Body-diode reverse recovery is published as trr = 268 ns typical and 402 ns maximum at IF = 28 A; the strict schema has no separate transient field for MOSFET body-diode recovery."
  ],
